A new paradigm for language models: Sigma is the first 3B/8B continuous diffusion LM that generates text by smoothly denoising 16-D token embeddings, not discrete tokens. 

Sigma matches or beats masked diffusion LMs on GSM8K, Minerva, HumanEval, and MBPP—achieving 84.5% GSM8K pass@1 and graceful accuracy at just 16 steps (78% GSM8K, 60% HumanEval). With distillation, a student model retains 70% MBPP at 32× speedup.

Key: classifier-free guidance + score temperature steer quality/diversity on the fly—minimal latency cost, maximal control. Instruction-tuned Sigma hits 89.2% GSM8K and outperforms on pass@k for coding/math, unlocking new potential for fast, steerable, and on-device generation.

